+- **Shared Worker reads (#414):** every non-user-initiated read of the Worker from the browser goes through `src/lib/worker-data.ts` (`workerData`, hook `useWorkerData` in `src/lib/use-worker-data.ts`), never a component's own `fetchWorker`. A read is keyed by route + the 0.05 degree cell (`cellKey` in `src/lib/cell-key.ts`, the Worker's `cell_key`, after `roundCoord`) + its other parameters; callers of one key share ONE in-flight request (never two per route+cell; one retry on a network error or 5xx, `retries: 0` where a caller owns its own retrying); `useWorkerData` reads the state FROM the store with `useSyncExternalStore` (the server and hydration render are always `loading`, so a warm browser store cannot cause a hydration mismatch, and an expired answer stays on screen while it is read again, and stays there if the refresh fails or comes back degraded); a good answer is kept in memory for a per-route time (`WORKER_DATA_TTL_MS`: weather 5 min, air quality / haze / grid 10 min, nearest METAR 5 min, reports 1 min, climate normals 1 h, monthly normals 6 h; nothing is kept forever); a failure is replayed for 20 s (60 s for a 429, longer with `Retry-After`) so a failing or rate-limited Worker is not asked on every remount; a degraded answer (`X-Weather-Provider: fallback`, `available: false`, `degraded: true`, aviation `status: "unavailable"`, a `/v1/geo` whose naming was skipped) is kept only briefly. A caller leaving (unmount, route change) stops WAITING; it never cancels the request. `LazySection` unmounts a section that scrolls far away and mounts it again, which used to repeat every fetch (one browser made about 150 calls in two minutes and was refused 429 by the per-IP limiter); now a cold place page makes at most 25 Worker calls (about 15) and a place already shown this session none (`src/lib/place-page-fetch-budget.test.ts`). While a place is read, up to four more forecast requests go out at idle to warm the next saved places (`PlaceController.warm`, rules in `src/lib/place-warm.ts`): one at a time, the Worker only through `fetchWorkerWeatherOnce` (never a direct provider call), none with Save-Data or offline, one on a low-memory device, paused for 60 s after a failure, and a warmed copy only takes a free slot in the controller's memory so it never pushes out a place the visitor opened. The owner accepted this cost (2026-11-04). The memory is the page's: a full document reload starts empty. Sections that fetch below the fold still wait until they are near the viewport. Failures come back typed (`WorkerFailure`: `rate_limited` | `timeout` | `server` | `offline` | `invalid`, with `retryAfterSeconds`)
 - **Live weather recovery (#414):** when the server could only send the seasonal estimate, `useLiveWeather` (`src/lib/use-live-weather.ts`, rules in `src/lib/live-fetch.ts`) fetches the live forecast at once and keeps at it: a failed attempt is retried after about 2 s, 5 s and 15 s (three retries after the first attempt; a page that already has live weather, whose fetch only feeds optional cards, retries once), a 429 waits for `Retry-After` (at most 60 s, `0` meaning the normal backoff; 30 s when the header is missing or the browser cannot read it, which is why the public API exposes `Retry-After` through CORS), timeouts and 5xx back off the same way, a 4xx other than 429 is not retried, offline waits for the browser's `online` event. The `online` event and the tab becoming visible each make one attempt (never while one is in flight, never twice within a second); nothing reloads the page (`reloadOnOnline: false` in the Serwist options, because the default `location.reload()` restarted the app on every reconnect). Every failure goes to `console.warn` through `logWarn` (route, status, kind, attempt, the slug coarsened) and to GA4 (`reportLiveWeatherFailure`); never coordinates or URLs. The first live forecast replaces the seed and clears the banner (`resolveDisplayedWeather`); "Try again" starts a fresh episode. Air quality is a separate read and cannot move the banner
 - **Device profile (`/v1/devices`):** a device's profile does not exist on the Worker until it is created. On a 404 for `GET` or `PATCH /v1/devices/{id}` the sync creates it ONCE with `POST /v1/devices` carrying the same `deviceId` (idempotent, not metered) and the device's current preferences (`src/lib/rxdb/device-profile.ts`); a second 404 right after a create leaves the device local-only for the session; failures back off 30 s doubling to 15 min and nothing is sent meanwhile; silent (no console output) and never blocks a render
 - User preferences (theme + selected activities) are persisted to localStorage via Zustand `persist` middleware under key `mukoko-weather-prefs`
